Communication is integral to any relationship, and we recognise that there are now more ways than ever for us to communicate effectively together. We will liaise with you in a variety of ways, including remote video or telephone meetings, letters, emails, through online communication portals and newsletters. You may at any time choose to change your preferences as to how we communicate with you.
Should you require us to make a reasonable adjustment in providing the advisory services to you , please speak to your financial adviser. Examples of reasonable adjustments may be the provision of a large print format pdf or documents provided in braille.
We are required by our regulators (the FCA ) to keep records of electronic communications with our clients in relation to the arranging of transactions in pensions, investments, and insurances that are categorised as financial instruments.
## CLIENT AGREEMENT
We advise clients who are based in the United Kingdom (UK), if you do not live in the UK, or are currently staying here but normally live abroad, there may be restrictions on how we can advise you . This also applies if you are currently staying in the UK and plan to move abroad or return from another country.  If any of these situations apply to you , please let us know immediately so that we can check we are in a position to act for you .
In order to provide the advisory services , we need to obtain and retain information about you . Where you fail to provide this information, we will likely be unable to provide the requested advisory services .  Additionally, we retain the right to refuse to offer advisory services to you .
We are not tax advisers and therefore recommend that you take specialist tax advice.
For the purposes of the FCA rules, you will be categorised and treated as a retail client .  This means you will be given the highest levels of protection available, including access to the Financial Ombudsman Service (subject to their eligibility criteria).
