pported**: The report states the critical yield is 2.94% and claims this is \"achievable given the past performance of your recommended funds.\" However, the switching research does not provide past performance data for the recommended fund to support this claim. The critical yield is a real figure (after 2% inflation adjustment), while any quoted past performance would be nominal, making a direct comparison problematic.\n\n(4) **Risk alignment rationale not fully evidenced**: The report asserts the current funds have \"risk level of 6\" which does not match the agreed Cautious Balanced profile of 4. The extraction notes an ambiguity: the existing holdings are \"Vanguard LifeStrategy 60% Equity (35.02%) Vanguard LifeStrategy 80% Equity (64.95%)\" — the 60% is typically risk level 5 and the 80% is typically risk level 6, creating ambiguity about the combined portfolio's actual risk level. The file does not provide explicit confirmation that the combined portfolio is risk level 6.\n\n(5) **Alternative options not adequately addressed**: The switching research [P9] ranks multiple options by maturity value. The third-ranked option is \"Aviva Pension Portfolio - Core Platform: Aviva Platform\" at 0.7% charges and £86,700 maturity value — identical to the new solution. The report does not explain why this option was not recommended, or why the new solution (ranked second at £86,700) is preferable to leaving the existing arrangement untouched (ranked first at £86,800).\n\n(6) **Professional oversight and fund range not evidenced as unavailable**: The report cites \"Professional Oversight\" and improved fund range as benefits of the switch. However, the file contains no evidence that professional oversight was unavailable under the existing Aviva arrangement, or that the existing fund range was inadequate. The Aviva plan information form [P10] indicates the plan has \"comprehensive investment choices\" and is on the Aviva Platform, suggesting these features were already available.\n\n(7) **Switching research models wrong existing product**: The switching research [P13] models the existing arrangement as \"Aviva Life & Pensions UK Limited - Current Aviva\" with \"Platform: None,\" but the policy research [P7] shows the client is already in \"Aviva Life & Pensions UK Limited - Pension Portfolio\" (AV2075926-001, opened 27/09/2013). The research does not analyse what is actually being recommended — an agency change plus a fund switch within the same plan, not a switch to a different product.\n\nThe guards do not explain these discrepancies. The charge analysis is on the same basis (like-for-like, before advice charges), the maturity values are on the same basis (mid growth 2.94%, age 60), and the switching research is the adviser's own document, not a different source with different assumptions. The report's own switching research contradicts the stated rationale that the switch produces lower costs and better outcomes.","citations":[{"passageId":"P17","source":"Suitability Report - Barnes.md","category":"I","quote":"Aviva Pension Portfolio - AV2075926-001 | 0.54% | £427 | +0.08% | +£63","cells":null},{"passageId":"P14","source":"Suitability Report - Barnes.md","category":"I","quote":"Based on information supplied by Aviva, our calculations show that the recommended fund strategy is 0.08% more expensive than your current plan. This means that your proposed plan will need to outperform your current plan by £63 in the first year (in monetary terms).","cells":null},{"passageId":"P6","source":"Pension switch report 16-12-2025 10-06.md","category":"G","quote":"Mid growth rate – (2.94%) | Existing pension: Projected value at age 60: £86,800 | New solution: Projected value at age 60: £86,700 | Effect of switching: £100 or 0.1% decrease","cells":null},{"passageId":"P9","source":"Pension Switching research report 16-12-2025 10-06.md","category":"G","quote":"1 | Existing Solution | 0.6% | £86,800 | 2 | New Solution | 0.7% | £86,700","cells":null},